{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QqwMniZq2i7MDZrBGhczPA","type":"tool_result","content":"# binary-swift-justice solver notes\n\nVARIANT AXIS: Mastery set count (2 on auto-mastery-d1a6613c, up to 5 x 31 MB on D8) -- main() now groups (answer_id, question) pairs with lib.common.group_by_set and solves each set in a fork ProcessPoolExecutor (sequential fallback on pool error, HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 disables); each set's delivery is still paired by contract sha256 via container_by_sha. Output identical to the sequential loop on all 9 cases.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change) -- the evidence.zip is all WinZip AE-2 (method 99, AES-256, deflate) and its 67 MB d08 Swift ELF was inflated serially through pyzipper (pure-Python HMAC-SHA1 + AES); unzip() now reads AES members directly (PBKDF2 + AES-CTR LE counter, pw-verifier check, no HMAC) in a thread pool, largest first, decrypt||inflate||sha256 pipelined for members > 8 MB, and returns Futures that group_members() resolves only for the group asked (falls back to the pyzipper reader on any miss). single 1.2 s -> 0.8 s local.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change; the 9.74 s was the harness's contention-measured Mastery estimate, real single = 0.5-0.6 s, 5-set Mastery 1.7-1.9 s pinned to 2 CPUs) -- per-set CPU trimmed: AE-2 members (CRC 0) skip the 67 MB crc32 pass, multi-set runs inflate the big member in one shot instead of the 3-thread pipeline (+20% CPU, ~0 wall), and the lazy deps (capstone/pefile/Cryptodome/lib.common) import once in the parent before forking. Floor: stock zlib inflate of the 67 MB d08 Swift ELF = 0.2 s/set.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\n====\nd12 FPC ELF: raw HCFG at 82928 (hcfg() now records raw offset) | patched\n====\n# Day 7 — Node by Node (script-analysis, node operation graphs)\n\nConcept: one evidence.zip with 61 members (PowerShell samples, JScript/Batch/VBScript/Python/Bash/Node operation\ngraphs); each graph decodes to a plan (steps/adapter/campaign/indicator) and is sorted into a role.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes. TT attempt 26b7da83 failed because its download was the GM body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B saved as evidence.zip, sha != contract sha256), so every field came out None/default. The harvested variants 49b73141 + 7d6f8d53 were already answered 469/469 by the current solver (spot-checked against the raw bytes; their expected.json is solver-derived, not GM-verified). Parse rule: if every artifact is a small `{\"error\": ...}` JSON, exit non-zero (solve.py now does) instead of guessing roles. The bytes-less case was removed from cases/ (still kept under time_trial/attempts/26b7da83).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none (Day 8 TT). The start returned 503 `training_rotation_invalid` with no attempt and no artifact, so there were no variant bytes. The solver answers the TT contract's 615 ids 615/615 on the single's bytes. Rule: a start error is an orchestrator retry, not a solver change.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"720e247d-3d33-4acd-9c1c-873819f50faf","uuid":"1b046128-ed10-4e49-8cda-d297476880ca","timestamp":"2026-10-12T23:20:09.652Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# binary-swift-justice solver notes\n\nVARIANT AXIS: Mastery set count (2 on auto-mastery-d1a6613c, up to 5 x 31 MB on D8) -- main() now groups (answer_id, question) pairs with lib.common.group_by_set and solves each set in a fork ProcessPoolExecutor (sequential fallback on pool error, HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 disables); each set's delivery is still paired by contract sha256 via container_by_sha. Output identical to the sequential loop on all 9 cases.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change) -- the evidence.zip is all WinZip AE-2 (method 99, AES-256, deflate) and its 67 MB d08 Swift ELF was inflated serially through pyzipper (pure-Python HMAC-SHA1 + AES); unzip() now reads AES members directly (PBKDF2 + AES-CTR LE counter, pw-verifier check, no HMAC) in a thread pool, largest first, decrypt||inflate||sha256 pipelined for members > 8 MB, and returns Futures that group_members() resolves only for the group asked (falls back to the pyzipper reader on any miss). single 1.2 s -> 0.8 s loc