y its storage location changes","   (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA array, Go/Rust rodata, base64'd in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift String literal in","-  `.rodata` on D8, base64 Nim/D string literal in `.rodata` on D9/D11). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND for its base64 form `SENGR...` (raw `HCFG` can also be a false hit inside code: check crc).","+  `.rodata` on D8, base64 Nim/D string literal in `.rodata` on D9/D11, RAW in FPC `.data` on D12). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND for its base64 form `SENGR...` (raw `HCFG` can also be a false hit inside code: check crc).","   The JSON also carries never-asked keys (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model on D7): parse the whole dict so a new `config_<key>` id is free."," - The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for a few `exact_text` fields (format,","   machine, disassembly, symbol). The question set grows each day (9 → 17 → 24 → 32 → 40 → 48 → 56 → 80 → 90 → 100 → 110 fields); old groups reuse the same bytes,","   but D8 BACKFILLED old groups to 10 ids each (new: has_symtab, has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable, xor_key_hex, hcfg_version, compression_methods)."," - The prompt's theme (Rust panics, D7 \"coroutine state machine\", D8 Swift \"protocols\", D9 Nim \"runtime fingerprints\") has NOT","   been asked since D4: the new group gets sha256, format, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex + 1-3 extra ids","-  (architecture D4-D5/D8-D11, hcfg_version D6-D7, elf_class/machine as INTEGERS D8-D9, `hcfg_offset` D9 + D11, `has_hcfg_section`","-  D10). D11 added NO new field at all (repeat of D9's hcfg_offset). Usually exactly ONE","+  (architecture D4-D5/D8-D12, hcfg_version D6-D7, elf_class/machine as INTEGERS D8-D9, `hcfg_offset` D9 + D11 + D12, `has_hcfg_section`","+  D10). D11/D12 added NO new field (D12 = hcfg_offset on a RAW blob). Usually exactly ONE","   never-seen field per day: grep the new group's ids against the solver's field table before anything else."," - Time Trial ≈ 6-16 s; Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies, 2 sets (7-12 s) through D7, 5 sets / 400-450 ids / 20-27 s on D8-D9,","-  3 sets / 300 ids / 28 s on D10, 3 sets / 330 ids / 30 s on D11 (TT 30 s too); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`.","+  3 sets / 300-360 ids / 28-30 s on D10-D12 (TT 30 s too); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`."," - **D10 RELAXED the label fields**: 36 ids are now `kind: pattern` whose syntax ACCEPTS equivalents (format: \"ELF or PE; case,","   ELF32/ELF64/PE32/PE32+ accepted\"; machine/architecture: \"standard tool or symbolic label, or decimal/hex code\"; e_type and","   endianness: symbolic constant / readelf label / numeric code; .NET format: any container_runtime token with CLI/CLR/.NET). D8-D9's"]},{"oldStart":35,"oldLines":10,"newStart":35,"newLines":10,"lines":["   base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim string literal in ELF `.rodata` on D8/D9): scan raw bytes for `HCFG`","   and for `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (base64 of `HCFG`, std or urlsafe), decode, accept only if crc32(plain) matches AND the JSON","   parses -- keep scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw `HCFG` decoys); never a fixed offset.","-- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in the member","-  (D9: the `S` of the base64 text). 30696 in all 6 D9 variants (single, TT, Mastery x5); D11 D ELF 368272 in all 5 variants","-  although each build's sha differed -- still compute it: record `m.start()` of","-  whichever scan hit (raw or base64) validated. For a raw-blob member it would presumably be the `HCFG` offset (unconfirmed).","+- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9/D11/D12)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in","+  the member: base64 form -> the `S` of `SENGR...` (D9 Nim 30696, D11 D 368272); RAW form -> the `H` of `HCFG` (D12 FPC 82928 =","+  0x143f0 in `.data`, GM-confirmed single