ger, Network Security Config","-  exception, locally stored credential in SharedPreferences). The theme was","+  exception, locally stored credential in SharedPreferences, client-side SQLite authorization state). The theme was","   flavour only: no day required exploiting it, even when the dex carried a matching stub class (d7 `WebViewBridge`,","   d8 `CleartextSession`, d9 `TrustEveryone`) or the prompt demanded a live action (\"replay it against the backend\"","   d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9 -- no CA/cert/network_security_config/TrustManager code was shipped)."," - What actually varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split,","-  hex, caesar+key, reverse again on d8, base64 again on d9, split again on d10, xor+key again on d11 -- codecs CAN repeat). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery","+  hex, caesar+key, reverse again on d8, base64 again on d9, split again on d10, xor+key again on d11, hex again on d12 -- codecs CAN repeat). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery","   sets) used the same codec. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: decode it from the first","   4 chars, which must become `ANS-`. The dex also holds the codec name as a `CODEC` string constant (d8, d9) and a","   `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` string."," - In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?","   case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM","-  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 9 days.","+  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 12 days."," - Expect escalation (inference, see reference/HARDENING.md): the answer may move into the dex, resources or a decrypt","   routine. `lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain for that case."," "]},{"oldStart":32,"