 not reliably grow with the set count). Only a deterministic solver survives these windows. The single_solve is untimed."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)"]},{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":6,"newStart":23,"newLines":11,"lines":["   147 chars (len%4==3) and its bytes happened to hold no `-`/`_`; the TT blob was len%4==0 (strict b64 also decodes it);","   mastery line 11 is 14 chars (`bi1tYXBsZS00OA` -> `n-maple-48`). Rule: `[A-Za-z0-9_-]+` with len%4 in {0,2,3} -> re-pad","   `'='*(-len%4)` and `urlsafe_b64decode`; len%4==1 is never base64. `lib.decode.decode_chunk` has this branch since D11.","+- **Direction (D12)** -- the text itself can be BACK-TO-FRONT: single/TT = the whole sentence reversed","+  (`56-ztrauq-tesnus-ytsez :retsaM emaG ...`), Mastery line 12 = a reversed slug tail (`69-enud-m` -> `m-dune-96`,","+  `21-teggun`, `36-yvi-ma`). Rot-N \"decodes\" such a line into plausible garbage (`69-fove-n`) -- 11/58 Mastery sets went","+  wrong that way. Parse rule (in `lib.decode.decode_chunk` since D12): a free-text fragment shaped `\\d{2,}-[A-Za-z][A-Za-z-]*`","+  is a reversed slug tail; otherwise take the reversal when it out-scores every rot-N on bigrams. 0 false hits on D3-D11."," - **Line wrapper** -- `NN<TAB>fragment` numbering; fragments split mid-word and join verbatim in number order."," - **Set count** -- grows by 5 per day (33 on day 7, 38 on day 8, 43 on day 9, 53 on day 11); the solver must loop over whatever the contract lists."," - **Delivery shape** -- mastery bytes arrive as ONE zip saved under the first member's name (`blob-01.txt`; the contract has NO"]},{"oldStart":42,"oldLines":6,"newStart":48,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `&#78;&#105;&#99;...` (only `&...;` tokens, no line end) | HTML entities: `python3 -c \"import html,sys;print(html.unescape(open(sys.argv[1]).read()))\" blob.txt` (covers `&#x..;` and named too) |"," | `\"\\u004e\\u0069...\"` (quoted, only `\\uXXXX`; prompt says \"escape\") | JSON string escapes: `python3 -c \"import json,sys;print(json.loads(open(sys.argv[1]).read()))\" blob.txt`. `lib.decode.decode_chunk` also gets it (generic fallback, ASCII only) |"," | `A-Z2-7=` | `base32 -d` |","+| Readable letters backwards, a slug at the START (`56-ztrauq-...`), `retsaM emaG` (prompt: \"wrong end\") | `rev blob.txt` (or `[::-1]`); a line `NN-word-x` in a numbered blob is a reversed slug tail. `decode_chunk` does it since D12 |"," | `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, NO trailing `=`, length %4 != 0 (prompt: \"URL-friendly\") | unpadded base64url: `python3 -c \"import base64,sys;t=open(sys.argv[1]).read().strip();print(base64.urlsafe_b64decode(t+'='*(-len(t)%4)).decode())\" blob.txt` (`base64 -d` errors on it); `lib.decode.decode_chunk` handles it |"," | Magic `PK\\x03\\x04` even if named `.txt` (mastery `blob-01.txt`) | `unzip -l`. It is a bundle of all sets `blob-01..NN.txt` |"," | Lines `01<TAB>...`, `02<TAB>...` | Strip the `NN\\t` prefix. Decode EACH line with its own encoding and concatenate without separators. Keep leading/trailing spaces |"]},{"oldStart":50,"oldLines":36,"newStart":57,"newLines":11,"lines":[" The generic path is `lib.decode.peel(data, accept)` (BFS over encodings) plus the day solvers in `challenges/day0N/warmups-*/solver/solve.py`. Each later solver re-checks every earlier day's cases."," "," ## Day by day","-**Day 1: A Little Based** (\"sixty-four is a good base\").","-- Artifact: 148-byte base64, one layer, decoded with `base64 -d` -> slug. CORRECT on the first submit.","-- The first 6 worker launches died in under 8 s with \"OAuth session expired\" (harness auth, not the challenge). The successful worker took about 95 s.","-- TT and mastery windows were 30 s. Mastery: 3 sets, each blob ONE line `01\\t<base64>`.","-- Mastery failed about 12 times in a row. The cause was the HARNESS, not the decode: the contract listed 3 downloads all named `blob.txt`, and `hctf artifact` saved only set1 (see challenges/day01/warmups-a-little-based/HELP.md). The solver now matches files by the contract's `artifacts[].sha256`.","-","-**Day 2: Half a Turn** (\"Thirteen steps forward\").","-- 108-byte ROT13 text -> `tr` rot13 -> slug. CORRECT first submit. Worker about 124 s, mostly harness bookkeeping. One stale start.json, overwritten by a re-start with no attempt_id, broke the completion check. It was restored from log.jsonl.","-- TT window 5 s. Several TT submits came back `expired` before the solver became the fast path.","-- Mastery 8 sets: a single download, a ZIP named `blob-01.txt` holding `blob-01..08.txt`. Each blob is 2 lines: base64, then rot13, joined verbatim.","-","-**Day 3: Hex Appeal** (\"Sixteen ... fingers\").","-- Plain hex string -> `xxd -r -p`. The single_solve took seconds via the reused generic solver (no worker log).","-- Mastery 13 sets x 3 lines (b64 / rot13 / hex), window 7 s.","-- Live mastery TIMEOUT: `english()` counted single letters, so a hex line (\"a\", \"e\" heavy) scored as English and was never decoded. The BFS took about 32 s per blob. Fixes: score only words of 2+ letters, add the fast `strict_line` path (strict hex -> strict b64 -> best rot-N, about 0.2 s for 13 sets), and cap the peel BFS at 0.6 s per question.","-","-**Day 4: Two of a Kind** (\"only two sides\").","-- Space-separated 8-bit binary. Reused solver, seconds.","-- Mastery 18 sets x 4 lines (+ binary line), window 7 s. Try binary before hex: 8-bit 0/1 groups are also valid hex.","-- Bug: the slug fragment \"er: <slug>\" got rot-shifted to \"an: ...\" because \"an\" is a common word. Rule now: a rot-N result must beat the UNSHIFTED text by >= 2.0 English score.","-","-**Day 5: By the Numbers** (\"reduced to numbers\").","-- Space-separated decimal ASCII codes. Reused solver, single_solve start->submit about 7 s per log.jsonl.","-- Mastery 23 sets x 5 lines (+ decimal), zip bundle again. TT window 6 s, mastery 7 s. CORRECT on attempt 1.","-","-**Day 6: Eight Is Enough** (\"counted on eight fingers. Again.\").","-- 109 zero-padded 3-digit octal codes, ONE layer. \"Again\" was NOT a second octal layer.","-- Worker about 355 s. Decoded in the first minute, the rest went to solver hardening.","-- Near-miss: a shell `while read` loop dropped the last token (the file has NO trailing newline), giving `...-3`. Checking against the \"two-digit number\" syntax caught it before submit.","-- Mastery 28 sets x 6 lines (+ octal), zip bundle. Octal and decimal both parse `101 110`. Tells: zero padding (`040`) means octal, a short unpadded token (`32`) means decimal. Decimal codes misread as octal come out ALL CAPS, so lowercase share helps the decision. Slug-only rot13 fragments are a near-tie on English score: in numbered blobs, give rot13 a prior.","+**Days 1-6** (base64, ROT13, hex, 8-bit binary, decimal, zero-padded octal): one layer each, solved in seconds-minutes.","+Lessons that still matter: D1 mastery failed ~12x because same-named `blob.txt` downloads overwrote each other (match by","+sha256); D3 mastery timed out when single letters/hex counted as English (score 2+-letter words, cap peel at 0.6 s); D4 a","+rot-N must beat the UNSHIFTED text by a margin (\"er:\" -> \"an:\"); D6 a shell `read` loop dropped the last token (no trailing","+newline), octal vs decimal = zero padding + lowercase share. Mastery from D2 on = ONE zip saved as `blob-01.txt`."," "," **Day 7: Percent Chance** (\"My address bar is having a moment\")."," - 318-byte blob, every byte percent-encoded (`%4e%69...`), ONE layer -> `urllib.parse.unquote` -> slug. Start->CORRECT 53 s, first submit."]},{"oldStart":126,"oldLines":9,"newStart":108,"newLines":22,"lines":[" - LIB (ratchet D11): `decode_chunk` gained the unpadded base64url branch; `decode_chunked` alone now reproduces all 53","   D11 mastery slugs (before: line 11 -> rot-N garbage `ry1jONRiPI00EQ`). Import it, don't re-type `_b64url`."," ","+**Day 12: Back at You** (\"Maybe we started at the wrong end.\" -- the sentence reversed).","+