ng the whole bundle. The value is self-describing, so verify it against `answer_format.syntax` and submit."," - Mastery ids are per set (`setN.message` style). Each question names `blob-0N.txt`, but the bytes may arrive as a zip member, as same-named `blob.txt` downloads, or de-duplicated (`blob_2.txt`). Map set -> file by sha256 from `contract[\"artifacts\"]` when present. When it is absent (day 7), open the zip and read member `blob-0N.txt`."," - No GM-side label grammar in this lane: the answer is a derived VALUE, never a synthetic label."," "]},{"oldStart":147,"oldLines":5,"newStart":142,"newLines":9,"lines":["   or build escapes with `chr(92)+'u%04x'`."," - Unpadded base64: tools that demand `len%4==0` reject it or (worse) a length-gated classifier skips it and a fallback","   returns plausible-looking rot-N text. Re-pad before decoding; `len%4==1` is the only impossible length.","+- Rot-N is the catch-all of `decode_chunk`, so ANY unrecognised plain-text transform (reversal on D12) comes back as","+  plausible-looking rot garbage, not as a failure. When a new day's line has no strict class, check `[::-1]` and other","+  plain transforms BEFORE trusting rot-N, and verify the slug's words read as English (`fove`, `ulev` don't).","+- A slow fallback (generic `peel` BFS per set) x 58 sets blows even a 30 s window: gate fallbacks on a hard per-set cap."," - Don't over-read the prompt: \"Again\" (day 6) was flavour, not a second layer. Decode what the bytes show."," - Don't contact anything beyond the GM. The decoded sentence states the answer outright."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/warmups.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0193XDsoMDNa1Ad3XuuxuiBc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
