{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfyD3QxgfNmQHjEDLYnWj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I merged the one worker proposal (for warmups) into `lib/decode.py`, added the day's GM-confirmed facts to `lib/knowledge.py` and `lib/playbook.py`, and logged day 12 in all five technique files. All five required checks pass (`test_orchestrate`, `test_day6_fixes`, `test_day7_fixes`, `test_codec`, `lib.refs.coverage 12`). Nothing was submitted or started, and nothing is committed.\n\n1. **`lib/decode.py`, warmups proposal accepted with a narrower rule:** `decode_chunk` now reads a fragment back-to-front instead of falling through to rot-N. That applies when the fragment looks like a reversed answer ending (`69-enud-m` → `m-dune-96`), or when its reversal reads more like English than every rot-N shift. The proposal's blanket \"never rot-N plain-looking text\" would have broken real rot13 lines, so I used this instead. Across all 1,275 warmups fragments from days 3–12, only the 56 day-12 ones change output, all to the right reading. `decode_chunked` alone now gets all 58 GM-confirmed day-12 Mastery answers; before the fix, rot-N garbage lost 11 of them, and the timed Mastery was lost to that plus an earlier solver timeout. I added a regression check to `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`.\n2. **`lib/knowledge.py` and `lib/playbook.py`, each GM-confirmed in single, Time Trial and Mastery:**\n   - **Binary:** when the config blob is stored raw rather than base64, `hcfg_offset` is the file offset of the `HCFG` magic itself (82928 in the Free Pascal build). Previously this case was marked unconfirmed.\n   - **Metadata:** `dotnet.mvid_guid` is written the way .NET prints GUIDs: first three groups byte-swapped, lowercase, hyphens, no braces (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le=...)`).\n   - **Scripting:** the role-to-ATT&CK table now notes it also covers AutoIt `.au3` files.\n3. **Technique logs:** each lane got a day-12 entry plus updated cues and pitfalls, and I compressed older entries. Files are now 150–243 lines; `script-analysis.md` (243) and `metadata-forensics.md` (221) are still above the ~200 target. Key additions:\n   - **Warmups:** a new \"Direction\" variant axis (text can be reversed) with its parse rule.\n   - **Binary:** the raw-blob offset rule, plus a pitfall: the copied solver's raw-scan path left the offset as `none`, which cost 2 wrong submits.\n   - **Metadata:** a `.NET` recipe for reading the MVID with the standard library only.\n   - **Scripting:** the AutoIt comment and descriptor syntax.\n   - **Mobile:** the \"SQLite cache\" was story only; the answer was still the hex-encoded puzzle file.\n4. **Rejected or not added:**\n   - No wrong answer spellings were rejected by the GM today, so no `*_REJECTED` entries were added.\n   - The metadata worker's ~90-line .NET metadata parser stays in its own solver, because the rules don't allow solver code in `lib/`.\n   - The old proposals carried in the binary and scripting `NOTES.md` files (fast AES unzip, GM error-body detection) come from earlier days and aren't day-12 facts, so I left them out.\n5. **Timings to CORRECT:** mobile ~4.5 s and warmups ~5 s (both answered by the previous day's solver as-is), scripting ~25 s, binary and metadata ~55 s. Every Time Trial and Mastery passed first try except warmups Mastery, which went CORRECT only in untimed practice with no Hall of Fame time."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":193718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"720e247d-3d33-4acd-9c1c-873819f50faf","uuid":"201e8ad3-4961-4882-abc6-8d935c850eb0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T23:26:49.340Z","request_id":"req_011CfyD3Q47uPJ6Hqt7BetMy"}
